# Cache rules for manual (drag-and-drop) deploys; netlify.toml carries the
# same rules for CLI deploys. Images and hashed assets never change at their
# URL; corpus data changes on redeploy at a URL that doesn't, so it has to be
# revalidated every time — a stale chunk in someone's browser cache would keep
# serving copy a redeploy was meant to take down. ETags make that a 304.
/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
